let's bring you some breaking news now  in a new yougov poll of conservative  party members has found that list trust  is the strong favorite to beat rishi  sunak in the race to be the next prime  minister well let's go live now to  westminster and to our deputy political  editor sam coats and sam a real boost  there for liz trust  that's right this is the first poll of  conservative party members that yougov  have done since we found out who is in  the last two that has to be uh that's  going to the conservative party  membership over the next few weeks and  here are the results  rishi sunak gets 38  of the  of the votes while liz truss is on 62 so  a pretty whopping lead for the foreign  secretary currently she is there for 24  percentage points ahead of her rival  rishi sunak this is an expanded lead  compared to just earlier this week you  can see that the 62 percent is up two  from a poll taken uh of tory party  members on monday tuesday uh rishi sunax  38 is down two uh compared to that poll  at the start of the week now that looks  like a very big hurdle for the former  chancellor to overcome  in the next few weeks ballots going out  in about a fortnight but look at the  toxicity of this race cap  who can't be trusted well liz trusts uh  18 of conservative party members say  that liz trust can't be uh trusted but  40  of tory party members say that rishi  sunak can't be trusted it seems like all  those stories of rishi sunak's betrayal  of boris johnson some of which stretch i  think a little bit of the  bounds of credibility and truth and the  relentless hammering he's had from some  mps and certain media outlets well  that's really rubbed off  and it makes it just that little bit  harder for the conservative party to  come back together in the event that  rishi sunak becomes prime minister at  the end of it which doesn't now look  like  the likely outcome but to give you a  sense of the breadth of uh liz truss's  support  she gets  the majority of the vote 