 it was ben wallace and  if we go back as far as january rishi  sunak had a commanding leave over yes  liz truss so certainly the conservative  party membership are volatile they have  been proven to change their minds and  they will go where the wind takes them  however right now this looks like a huge  huge mountain forces tonight to climb if  the polling is anything to go by are  there any clues in the data as to why  tory party members are backing liz truss  over ishino i think there's a couple of  things yes one of the significant things  that we've been finding when we talk to  conservative party members is they're  looking for honesty integrity and a  return to conventional conservative  values so what does that mean well it's  big trouble for issue tsunak if 40 of  the conservative party membership don't  think he can be trusted it's also a big  problem i think that liz trust is able  to or is getting out on a platform and  saying she's prioritizing tax cuts  straight away a return to that reduction  in the involvement of the state in the  economy registration sunac is saying he  wants to keep taxes where they are for  now deal with inflation and then look at  tax cuts so certainly liz choice is kind  of singing from the same hymn sheet if  you like conservative item members and i  think that's costing risky sunk at the  minute with them do you think that the  data shows that there's just not enough  excitement around richie sunak's policy  program it seems like he's promising jam  tomorrow she's promising jam today is  that having an impact i think it  absolutely is yes as we say these  conservative conventional conservative  values are coming up time and time again  when we talk to the conservative party  members we let them tell us in their own  words what they'd like to see and they  were talking to us about tax cuts they  were talking about a reduction in the  amount of government spending those  exactly the sort of things that liz  trust is campaigning on right now and  that makes difficult for rishi sunak  final question the rishi suna  campaign tell us time and again that he  can beat kierstarma better than liz  trust is that true well at the minute  our current favorability ratings for  both of these politicians so the amount  of people that say they have a positive  opinion minus the amount that saying  that having negative opinion is at minus  31 each so i don't think there's much  evidence at all that either of them are  going to fare much better at the moment  but of course those that's a very  hypothetical question we have to see  much closer to the time when the public  starts to get really thinking about  general elections and who the candidates  actually are patrick english thank you  very much indeed uh that final port  critical rishi sunax team tell you he's  better place to win a general election  not clear that that's true from the  evidence  sam thank you that's sam coates our  deputy political editor in westminster  and just a reminder that in two weeks  time we'll see those two candidates go  head-to-head here on sky news in a live  televised debate k burley will be  hosting it all on thursday the 4th of  august at 8 00 pm

